.TH LIANLI-DAEMON 1 "" "Lian Li Linux"
.SH NAME
lianli-daemon \- control supported Lian Li hardware
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lianli-daemon
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B lianli-daemon capabilities
.br
.B lianli-daemon
.RI [ options ]
.B lcd clean
.RI [ "\-\-device-id ID" ]
.RI [ "\-\-minutes N" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The daemon controls fans, lighting and LCD media and serves the desktop client
through a Unix socket. Use the GUI service controls to select one user or system
daemon. Packaged hardware services are not enabled on a fresh installation.
Run hardware control under the selected unprivileged account.
.PP
Desktop display capture additionally requires
.BR lianli-session (1)
in the active graphical login. Ordinary hardware control does not require the GUI.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " PATH
Use the specified configuration file.
.TP
.BI "\-\-socket " PATH
Use the specified IPC socket.
.TP
.B \-\-system
Select system-service mode and default paths. This option does not change the
process account.
.TP
.BI "\-\-log-level " LEVEL
Set logging to error, warn, info, debug or trace. Default: info.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show command help. Subcommands also accept this option.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the application version.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B capabilities
Print build and IPC capabilities without loading configuration or accessing hardware.
.TP
.B lcd clean
Request pixel conditioning through the selected daemon's IPC socket.
The optional device ID limits the target; otherwise all applicable LCDs are targeted.
Duration defaults to 30 minutes; positive values above 255 are limited to 255.
This command changes LCD output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lianli/config.json
User configuration; defaults to ~/.config/lianli/config.json.
.TP
.I /var/lib/lianli/config.json
Default system configuration.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lianli-daemon.sock
Default user socket; /tmp is used if XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset.
.TP
.I /run/lianli/lianli-daemon.sock
Default system socket.
.SH SIGNALS
SIGINT and SIGTERM request orderly shutdown. Stop the selected service before
starting a replacement daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lianli-gui (1),
.BR lianli-control (1),
.BR lianli-session (1)
.PP
https://github.com/sgtaziz/lian-li-linux/tree/main/docs
